{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And it shall be ready in the morning, and you shall go up in the morning to Mount Sinai.</b> It should have said 'and it shall be ready in the morning and you shall go up to Mount Sinai,' but Scripture alludes to the attribute of the morning: it says, 'and it shall be ready in the morning' — to receive the power of the morning, which is the attribute of mercy — 'and you shall go up in the morning.' This is the matter of what is written (Psalms 5:4): ״YHWH, in the morning You hear my voice; in the morning I arrange my prayer to You and watch.״ David, peace be upon him, prayed to the attribute of mercy, which is the power of the morning, that He would hear his voice every morning that he would arrange before Him."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:06:48.227864831Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}